WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.264
Wang Shenzhi, at about fifty, founded the kingdom of Min in Fujian and became its king.

00:00:06.614 --> 00:00:13.742
He encouraged the farmers to open up the land; the paddies were a sheet of green, and the harvest grew better year by year.

00:00:14.092 --> 00:00:21.964
The harbor was filled with great sailing ships, and overseas trade brought goods of every kind.

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:27.666
The ships were loaded full of tea, silk and porcelain.

00:00:28.016 --> 00:00:34.496
The city's markets bustled, the people lived in contentment, and Min grew ever richer and stronger.

00:00:34.846 --> 00:00:38.398
People came and went along the street in extraordinary bustle.

00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:43.836
The people, remembering his deeds with gratitude, honored him as the 'King who Opened Min'.

00:00:44.186 --> 00:00:49.346
This title was the people's heartfelt thanks.

00:00:49.696 --> 00:00:55.744
Wang Shenzhi's story is a model of regional development in the history of the Ten Kingdoms.

